WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.713 --> 00:00:02.896
- Have the fortitude to do the right thing

00:00:02.896 --> 00:00:04.417
not the easy thing.

00:00:04.417 --> 00:00:07.378
Don't be somebody's lap dog or sycophant.

00:00:07.378 --> 00:00:09.992
I think I spend probably 50
or 60% of my time learning,

00:00:09.992 --> 00:00:12.100
reading, talking to people, traveling.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.512
Go to work at a place where
you respect the people,

00:00:14.512 --> 00:00:17.107
you think the company has
the kind of culture you like,

00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:18.619
it's going to grow, it's to be ambitious.

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:20.105
Do you want to be a winner

00:00:20.105 --> 00:00:22.041
then compare yourself to the best,

00:00:22.041 --> 00:00:24.332
acknowledge that will never
happen without hard work.

00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:26.166
If you're not prepared for tough times

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:28.041
you're not going to be,
you can't like get prepared

00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:29.278
when times get tough.

00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:30.501
If I do well here I
can help our employees,

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.920
help our clients, help our communities.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.637
Never fool yourself into
thinking that your success

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:36.202
is yours alone.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.114
- He's an American business executive.

00:00:38.114 --> 00:00:42.214
- He's a chairman, president
and CEO of JP Morgan Chase.

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:44.845
- He has an estimated net
worth of 1.1 billion dollars.

00:00:44.845 --> 00:00:47.006
- He's Jamie Dimon and
here's my take on his

00:00:47.006 --> 00:00:49.173
top ten rules for success.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.975
- It takes courage to be accountable.

00:00:54.975 --> 00:00:57.888
Throughout my life, throughout
this crisis of the past

00:00:57.888 --> 00:01:01.029
four years I have seen many
people embarrass themselves

00:01:01.029 --> 00:01:02.547
by failing to stand up,

00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:05.329
(mumbling) and acting like lemons

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:07.611
by simply going along with the pack.

00:01:07.611 --> 00:01:11.185
I also saw plenty of people
under enormous pressure

00:01:11.185 --> 00:01:13.757
who always did the right thing.

00:01:13.757 --> 00:01:16.438
Graduates, you will soon
leave this wonderful community

00:01:16.438 --> 00:01:19.986
and venture into a new world,
you're ready for new jobs,

00:01:19.986 --> 00:01:22.905
new opportunities and new lives.

00:01:22.905 --> 00:01:26.356
Along the way you're going
to face a lot of pressure.

00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:28.368
Pressure to go along, to get along,

00:01:28.368 --> 00:01:30.330
to toe the line, to look the other way

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.042
when you see things that aren't right.

00:01:33.042 --> 00:01:35.094
And pressure to do things simply because

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.644
everybody else is doing them.

00:01:37.644 --> 00:01:39.745
Never give in to that pressure.

00:01:39.745 --> 00:01:42.606
Have the fortitude to do the right thing,

00:01:42.606 --> 00:01:43.685
not the easy thing.

00:01:43.685 --> 00:01:47.160
Don't be somebody's lap dog or sycophant.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.102
Have the courage to speak the truth

00:01:49.102 --> 00:01:51.543
even when it is unpopular.

00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:54.464
And have the courage to
put yourself on the line,

00:01:54.464 --> 00:01:56.433
to strive for something meaningful

00:01:56.433 --> 00:02:00.177
and even to risk would be
an embarrassing failure.

00:02:00.177 --> 00:02:03.545
I think Teddy Roosevelt understood
this to be a century ago

00:02:03.545 --> 00:02:05.583
when he said, and I quote,

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.820
"It is not the critic who counts.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.621
"Not the man who points out
how the strong man stumbles

00:02:11.621 --> 00:02:14.736
"or where the doer deeds
could have done them better.

00:02:14.736 --> 00:02:18.142
"The credit belongs to
the man, now the woman,

00:02:18.142 --> 00:02:20.084
"who is actually in the arena

00:02:20.084 --> 00:02:23.547
"whose face is marred by
dust and sweat and blood,

00:02:23.547 --> 00:02:26.423
"who strives valiantly, who airs,

00:02:26.423 --> 00:02:28.817
"who comes up short again and again

00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:32.635
"because there is no effort
without airing and shortcoming.

00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:35.213
"But it does actually
strive to do the deeds

00:02:35.213 --> 00:02:38.774
"who knows great enthusiasms,
the great devotions,

00:02:38.774 --> 00:02:41.607
"who spends himself in a worthy cause.

00:02:41.607 --> 00:02:45.477
"Who at the best knows
in the end of the triumph

00:02:45.477 --> 00:02:47.961
"of high achievement and who at the worst

00:02:47.961 --> 00:02:51.194
"if he fails, at least
fails while daring greatly

00:02:51.194 --> 00:02:54.077
so that his place shall
never be with those cold

00:02:54.077 --> 00:02:57.833
"and timid souls who know
neither victory nor defeat."

00:02:57.833 --> 00:03:00.024
Learning is a lifelong thing.

00:03:00.024 --> 00:03:01.962
It doesn't end at Harvard Business School.

00:03:01.962 --> 00:03:03.548
It's your responsibility, I think,

00:03:03.548 --> 00:03:05.537
if you're in any profession at all

00:03:05.537 --> 00:03:08.231
you have to do it
consistently all the time.

00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:11.511
I think I spend probably 50
or 60% of my time learning,

00:03:11.511 --> 00:03:14.073
reading, talking to people, traveling.

00:03:14.073 --> 00:03:15.884
It's the only way to keep on top

00:03:15.884 --> 00:03:17.776
of this global world of ours.

00:03:17.776 --> 00:03:19.817
And it's even tougher now because of the

00:03:19.817 --> 00:03:22.839
globality of the businesses
you're all going to deal in.

00:03:22.839 --> 00:03:25.229
How, reading is the most important one.

00:03:25.229 --> 00:03:27.306
But the second one,
which is often forgotten,

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.812
is talking to other people.

00:03:28.812 --> 00:03:32.112
You can learn more from
speaking to people in 15 minutes

00:03:32.112 --> 00:03:34.263
then if you spend your
life doing something.

00:03:34.263 --> 00:03:36.897
They can explain it to
you and you can learn from

00:03:36.897 --> 00:03:38.036
watching people.

00:03:38.036 --> 00:03:41.606
You also are going to
learn by, I'm going to

00:03:41.606 --> 00:03:44.490
call it imitation, but by
watching other very good people

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.852
and how they operate in
difficult circumstances.

00:03:46.852 --> 00:03:48.726
I learned a lot of things, what not to do,

00:03:48.726 --> 00:03:52.182
and a lot of things what to
do by watching other people.

00:03:52.182 --> 00:03:54.256
Go to work at a place where
you respect the people,

00:03:54.256 --> 00:03:56.890
you think the company has
the kind of culture you like,

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:59.188
it's going to grow, it's
going to be ambitious

00:03:59.188 --> 00:04:01.596
and your career will
take who knows what path.

00:04:01.596 --> 00:04:04.249
Then do think ahead a
couple of jobs so that

00:04:04.249 --> 00:04:07.149
you're always thinking maybe
what I might want to do next.

00:04:07.149 --> 00:04:08.490
And you know in one point life you have to

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.542
make a vertical switch.

00:04:09.542 --> 00:04:11.277
Or in some point life may get fired

00:04:11.277 --> 00:04:12.888
like some of us have been.

00:04:12.888 --> 00:04:14.660
And those those are hard things but they

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.822
could be very good things.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.004
So I also find some people
said that's what they want.

00:04:18.004 --> 00:04:19.554
And they're looking up
those hundred stairs

00:04:19.554 --> 00:04:21.463
and they're always measuring
how quickly they're going

00:04:21.463 --> 00:04:22.950
versus their friend.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.148
You're not doing the right thing,

00:04:24.148 --> 00:04:26.155
you're not enjoying your job

00:04:26.155 --> 00:04:28.562
It takes a lot of luck to get to that top

00:04:28.562 --> 00:04:31.786
rung sometimes and and
if you're really good

00:04:31.786 --> 00:04:33.137
you'll probably get there.

00:04:33.137 --> 00:04:34.222
It may not be at that company,

00:04:34.222 --> 00:04:35.358
it may be somewhere else.

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:37.365
I tell you enjoy your life.

00:04:37.365 --> 00:04:39.391
Enjoy every step of it and
don't don't worry too much

00:04:39.391 --> 00:04:40.852
about that kind of ambition.

00:04:40.852 --> 00:04:42.264
Many of you already have dealt with some

00:04:42.264 --> 00:04:43.379
very difficult times.

00:04:43.379 --> 00:04:45.351
So this is no different than some of you

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.934
already dealt with.

00:04:47.849 --> 00:04:50.156
When you fail it's okay to get depressed,

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:52.610
it's okay to cry, it's okay to go home,

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:55.456
it's okay to blame others for a while.

00:04:55.456 --> 00:05:00.221
But eventually you have to
get over it and move on.

00:05:00.221 --> 00:05:02.840
The greatest people who
have ever walked this planet

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.766
and I'm talking, I'm not
talking business people,

00:05:04.766 --> 00:05:07.574
I'm talking about people like
Nelson Mandela and Abe Lincoln

00:05:07.574 --> 00:05:10.723
constantly had setbacks
in life and failures.

00:05:10.723 --> 00:05:13.359
Constantly, it happens
all the time in business.

00:05:13.359 --> 00:05:15.015
And some of your success
will be how you deal with

00:05:15.015 --> 00:05:18.128
the failure, not how you
deal with the success.

00:05:18.128 --> 00:05:20.781
When I get introduced
I always get introduced

00:05:20.781 --> 00:05:23.939
that 1998 I was the president of Citigroup

00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:26.089
and in 2000 I took over Bank One.

00:05:26.089 --> 00:05:28.272
I was fired in 1998.

00:05:28.272 --> 00:05:30.598
So I went a little bit
of experience like this.

00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:32.681
And it's a painful thing.

00:05:33.549 --> 00:05:35.750
My boss who I had worked
for 15 years called me in

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.583
and said, 'We want you to resign."

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:42.614
To which I said, "Okay."

00:05:42.614 --> 00:05:45.246
I went home I told my wife and children.

00:05:45.246 --> 00:05:47.596
I called my wife up and
said, "Judy I'm going to

00:05:47.596 --> 00:05:48.519
"tell you something.

00:05:48.519 --> 00:05:49.630
"I'm not kidding."

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.792
Because I always make jokes
about things like that.

00:05:52.792 --> 00:05:54.603
But I wanted to make
sure the kids were fine.

00:05:54.603 --> 00:05:56.498
I went home my three wonderful daughters,

00:05:56.498 --> 00:05:58.376
they were much younger then.

00:05:58.376 --> 00:06:00.378
I said, the oldest, the youngest one said,

00:06:00.378 --> 00:06:02.518
"Dad do we have to sleep on the streets?"

00:06:02.518 --> 00:06:04.123
(laughing)

00:06:04.123 --> 00:06:06.364
I said, "No hon, we're okay."

00:06:06.364 --> 00:06:08.972
The middle one who had just
graduated Barnard said,

00:06:08.972 --> 00:06:10.715
"Dad can I still go to college?"

00:06:10.715 --> 00:06:12.301
I said, "Yes dear, you can."

00:06:12.301 --> 00:06:14.084
And I knew things were
fine when the oldest one

00:06:14.084 --> 00:06:16.229
who was going to Harvard
Business School said,

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:18.746
"Dad, can I have that
little cell phone you have.

00:06:18.746 --> 00:06:19.934
"You won't be needing it."

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:22.184
(laughing)

00:06:23.826 --> 00:06:26.652
I remind people when you fail at something

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.486
it's your, I told people at Citigroup

00:06:28.486 --> 00:06:31.256
it's my net worth, not my self-worth.

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:32.608
And I was able to move on

00:06:32.608 --> 00:06:34.101
and yes it was difficult.

00:06:34.101 --> 00:06:36.501
I did call my boss a year later.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.468
He did not call me, I called him and said,

00:06:38.468 --> 00:06:39.875
"It's time to break bread."

00:06:39.875 --> 00:06:41.499
We went to lunch together.

00:06:41.499 --> 00:06:43.865
I told them that entity did
the right thing for Citigroup

00:06:43.865 --> 00:06:45.711
which is pretty obvious at this point.

00:06:45.711 --> 00:06:48.301
But.
(laughing)

00:06:48.301 --> 00:06:51.868
But, I told him the mistakes I made

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:54.942
and was 40 60 or 60 40 wasn't important.

00:06:54.942 --> 00:06:57.448
I wanted to learn from the experience

00:06:57.448 --> 00:06:58.473
and move on.

00:06:58.473 --> 00:06:59.734
If you want to be a winner

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.594
then compare yourself to the best

00:07:01.594 --> 00:07:05.492
and acknowledge that will
never happen without hard work.

00:07:05.492 --> 00:07:09.080
Abe Lincoln used to say,
"Good things may come

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.512
"to those who wait."

00:07:10.512 --> 00:07:14.272
"But only those things
left by those who hustle."

00:07:14.272 --> 00:07:17.430
If you want to be a
leader, act like a leader.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.498
If you want to be respected and trusted

00:07:19.498 --> 00:07:23.349
then demonstrate you deserve
it by earning it every day.

00:07:23.349 --> 00:07:26.848
If you want to be known as
honest, not telling lies

00:07:26.848 --> 00:07:28.050
is not sufficient.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.097
Don't even shave the truth.

00:07:30.097 --> 00:07:32.276
And make sure your friends and colleagues

00:07:32.276 --> 00:07:34.504
will always bring you back to Earth

00:07:34.504 --> 00:07:36.174
when you, like we all do at times,

00:07:36.174 --> 00:07:37.637
for deceiving yourself.

00:07:37.637 --> 00:07:40.078
You know you all your
management is I think

00:07:40.078 --> 00:07:41.453
it's kind of relentless process.

00:07:41.453 --> 00:07:43.415
So I guess first, like someone said,

00:07:43.415 --> 00:07:45.850
we would have, we're
changing the crisis versus

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:46.855
before nothing.

00:07:46.855 --> 00:07:49.239
It's like, if you're not
prepared for tough times

00:07:49.239 --> 00:07:51.331
you're not going to be you
can't like get prepared

00:07:51.331 --> 00:07:52.622
when times get tough.

00:07:52.622 --> 00:07:54.828
Like you need the army
before the war starts.

00:07:54.828 --> 00:07:56.411
And so that means a disciplined group,

00:07:56.411 --> 00:07:57.244
they know what they're doing.

00:07:57.244 --> 00:08:00.438
The only real difference is
that the (mumbling) committee

00:08:00.438 --> 00:08:02.374
used to meet once a
week for a couple hours.

00:08:02.374 --> 00:08:05.220
And in the crisis it met
at seven AM, 12 lunch time,

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.248
five o'clock, 10 o'clock,
five AM, if it had to.

00:08:09.248 --> 00:08:12.126
24/7 for six straight months.

00:08:12.126 --> 00:08:13.700
And we had to say it
wasn't very formal we said,

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.625
hey if you've got a
problem go to the meeting

00:08:15.625 --> 00:08:17.281
and bring the people you got to have.

00:08:17.281 --> 00:08:18.800
And everyone shares the reports,

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:19.938
that shares the information.

00:08:19.938 --> 00:08:21.192
That tries to react very quickly.

00:08:21.192 --> 00:08:23.984
There is already a book on you.

00:08:23.984 --> 00:08:26.739
That book is already being written.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.665
And if I spoke to your
teachers, your friends,

00:08:28.665 --> 00:08:30.271
your professionals, your parents

00:08:30.271 --> 00:08:32.166
I would know whether you're trusted,

00:08:32.166 --> 00:08:34.345
how you work with your ethical.

00:08:34.345 --> 00:08:36.643
I would know so much about
you you'd be shocked.

00:08:36.643 --> 00:08:38.298
I don't even have to meet you.

00:08:38.298 --> 00:08:40.896
So that book is already growing.

00:08:40.896 --> 00:08:41.729
You should you write the
book you want the way

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:43.860
you want it to be written.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.190
You actually have that choice

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:49.023
and you can do it as you want now.

00:08:50.713 --> 00:08:52.602
Don't let others write it.

00:08:52.602 --> 00:08:54.608
And when you get caught in situations

00:08:54.608 --> 00:08:56.048
that you're uncomfortable

00:08:56.048 --> 00:08:58.904
I remember I worked at a
company not far from here.

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:00.562
And I remember I was asked to do something

00:09:00.562 --> 00:09:02.396
I didn't want to do, I might tell you,

00:09:02.396 --> 00:09:03.626
you'll take this advice.

00:09:03.626 --> 00:09:05.050
You can always quit.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.773
It's your responsibility
whether you accept

00:09:07.773 --> 00:09:08.894
to do something or not.

00:09:08.894 --> 00:09:11.404
And it will be in that
book written on you.

00:09:11.404 --> 00:09:14.498
- You had a major life-changing event,

00:09:14.498 --> 00:09:15.725
how are you doing?

00:09:15.725 --> 00:09:17.234
- I'm doing fine thank you.

00:09:17.234 --> 00:09:19.309
So far so good, I get tested all the time.

00:09:19.309 --> 00:09:20.878
- How has it changed you at all?

00:09:20.878 --> 00:09:22.224
How has it impacted you?

00:09:22.224 --> 00:09:24.100
- It didn't change my value system which

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.108
I've always literally family first,

00:09:26.108 --> 00:09:28.649
country and humanity second.

00:09:28.649 --> 00:09:31.387
Because they go hand in hand to me.

00:09:31.387 --> 00:09:33.488
But I think this country
still is the leading

00:09:33.488 --> 00:09:34.427
beacon in the world.

00:09:34.427 --> 00:09:36.036
If you actually travel around the world

00:09:36.036 --> 00:09:37.264
you'd feel that way too.

00:09:37.264 --> 00:09:38.937
And you know third is the job.

00:09:38.937 --> 00:09:40.271
But this is the best I can do.

00:09:40.271 --> 00:09:42.331
So if I do well here I
can help our employees,

00:09:42.331 --> 00:09:44.474
I can help our clients,
all of our communities.

00:09:44.474 --> 00:09:47.486
And the only real change
is that which I think it's

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.075
just a good life lesson is that

00:09:49.075 --> 00:09:51.788
I don't necessary assume I'm
going to live for 10 years.

00:09:51.788 --> 00:09:53.779
And you want to live very deliberately.

00:09:53.779 --> 00:09:56.014
Like, why are you doing this?

00:09:56.014 --> 00:09:57.518
Because you want to end every day and say,

00:09:57.518 --> 00:09:58.687
that was a good day.

00:09:58.687 --> 00:10:01.170
But I always tell people
it is it is your job

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:03.775
to take care of your, if
you have a job you know

00:10:03.775 --> 00:10:05.625
and we all spend a lot of time there.

00:10:05.625 --> 00:10:08.529
But your job it takes you
of your mind, your spirit,

00:10:08.529 --> 00:10:10.293
your body, your soul and your family.

00:10:10.293 --> 00:10:11.453
And you've got to take
that officially, so I do.

00:10:11.453 --> 00:10:13.779
I've always taken my vacations,

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:15.336
I've always had my family trips.

00:10:15.336 --> 00:10:17.657
I always you know cut
something short for the family.

00:10:17.657 --> 00:10:20.790
This phone 24/7 is used for
emergencies and children

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.844
and my wife, that's it.

00:10:22.844 --> 00:10:26.927
It takes humility and
humanity to be accountable.

00:10:27.939 --> 00:10:31.739
We all stand on the shoulders
of those who came before us.

00:10:31.739 --> 00:10:35.526
Humility is the realization
that those who came before

00:10:35.526 --> 00:10:36.950
pave the way.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.707
Never fool yourself into
thinking that your success

00:10:39.707 --> 00:10:41.665
is yours alone.

00:10:41.665 --> 00:10:44.475
Your success is the
result of your parents,

00:10:44.475 --> 00:10:46.963
the family who sacrificed
to give you a better life.

00:10:46.963 --> 00:10:49.352
Your professors and
administrators who helped you

00:10:49.352 --> 00:10:52.331
get through your time your Syracuse.

00:10:52.331 --> 00:10:56.586
Your friends, neighbors,
those who encouraged you.

00:10:56.586 --> 00:10:58.694
In fact this wonderful country
whose bounties we all benefit

00:10:58.694 --> 00:11:02.923
from was built by so many people
who made endless sacrifices

00:11:02.923 --> 00:11:05.122
often the ultimate sacrifice

00:11:05.122 --> 00:11:07.891
before most of us were even born.

00:11:07.891 --> 00:11:10.137
There's important to
respect what they have done

00:11:10.137 --> 00:11:11.749
and to be grateful for it.

00:11:11.749 --> 00:11:13.373
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:13.373 --> 00:11:15.457
- [Woman] We made this video because

00:11:15.457 --> 00:11:16.549
female foot kisser asked us to.

00:11:16.549 --> 00:11:17.921
If there's someone else
you'd like us a profile

00:11:17.921 --> 00:11:19.574
leave a message in the comments below.

00:11:19.574 --> 00:11:21.490
- We'd also love to know
which of the top ten rules

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.027
hit you the hardest and why.

00:11:23.027 --> 00:11:25.653
Leave in the comments and
we'll join in the discussion.

00:11:25.653 --> 00:11:29.025
Thank you so much for
watching, continue to believe

00:11:29.025 --> 00:11:30.942
and we'll see you soon.

